From: RMF <65404870+RMF112018@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 03:25:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Phase B 4th corrective (C4/code): atomic write-lock ownership
 + busy-aware fail-closed moved transitions (PB-010)

Fourth corrective on phase-b-source-index-architecture-completion, base
0464e347; preserves 80b4d13d, e488136f, 0464e347 (no amend). Closes the AEOS
FAIL/NO-GO PB-010 on the third commit. Evidence lands in a separate,
non-circular evidence-only commit (E5).

Root cause: apply_owned_confirmed_same_root_move proved ownership with a
read-only SELECT inside `with transaction(c)`, but the shared transaction()
helper never emits BEGIN and the connection uses isolation_level='' (implicit
BEGIN fires only before the first DML). The SELECT held no write lock, so a
requeue_stuck+reclaim could commit between the SELECT and the first source DML
and a stale attempt mutated under a lost claim.

Fix (scoped to the owned-move op + its indexer caller; shared transaction()
and global connection config unchanged):
- Ownership is proven by a guarded WRITE as the first statement
  (UPDATE ... SET updated_at=? WHERE event_id=? AND status='processing'
  AND attempts=?). The DML takes the RESERVED write lock immediately, so
  ownership and the source mutation share one write transaction; rowcount
  reflects ownership at lock-acquisition time (0 -> claim_conflict, no
  mutation). The write also refreshes the stuck lease.
- Pre-index event_is_owned SELECT replaced by a guarded heartbeat_owned_event
  (re-proves ownership AND refreshes the lease before expensive reindexing).
- is_sqlite_busy classifies SQLite BUSY/LOCKED by the PRIMARY result code
  (masking extended codes via & 0xFF), with a narrow message fallback; only
  busy/locked is retryable, every other OperationalError stays an error.
- defer_event and complete_owned_event are busy-aware (return db_busy on
  contention). Every moved transition (move guard, heartbeat, defer, terminal
  complete/skip, exhaustion, guarded exception path) is fail-closed: BUSY/LOCKED
  leaves the event 'processing' for requeue_stuck -- never a false terminal,
  never an unguarded fallback.

Tests (tests/test_source_index_moved_drain.py): all four orderings
(reclaim-before-guard -> claim_conflict; guard-before-reclaim -> B blocked at
the mutation boundary via a two-connection spy; reclaim-after-move ->
pre-index heartbeat conflict, no stale indexing; owner retained -> indexing
proceeds), busy-through-defer recoverable, exhaustion+busy-terminal
recoverable, non-busy OperationalError terminal, is_sqlite_busy primary+
extended classification, and controlled-timestamp lease-refresh. Contention
connections roll back + close in finally; stuck recovery is deterministic
(seeded lease). Full moved-drain suite green; ruff + mypy clean on the touched
modules.

No push / PR / deploy / prod DB / watcher activation / prod migration.

